    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "b7c00465_2750e1ab",
        "filename": "drivers/trusty/trusty-log.c",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 648,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000205
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-01-26T01:49:59Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Why not allow 1 page? The trusty code should support it with a 1/2 page log which is still a power of 2. (although, you would then need to use the _compat function below.",
      "revId": "d4f919f386d0d049c2d34f057d0d4db4e1f887f7",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "f0729703_74dd9ae6",
        "filename": "drivers/trusty/trusty-log.c",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 648,
      "author": {
        "id": 1001525
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-01-26T03:37:50Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I misunderstood the size requirement. I thought the log buffer needed to be a power-of-two number of pages, but apparently it\u0027s power-of-two number of bytes. I should have checked...\nWhy would using one page need the compat function though? The non-compat trusty_share_memory() seems to support using 1 page just fine.",
      "parentUuid": "b7c00465_2750e1ab",
      "revId": "d4f919f386d0d049c2d34f057d0d4db4e1f887f7",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "8dd5cd73_21201e7e",
        "filename": "drivers/trusty/trusty-log.c",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 648,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000205
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-01-26T04:00:22Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "It does, but sharing 1 page will work even if the trusty api version is \u003c TRUSTY_API_VERSION_MEM_OBJ. In that case, the the trusty log implementation  expects a different value than what trusty_share_memory provides. trusty_share_memory_compat will perform a conversion for that compatibility path. If you share more than one page, trusty_share_memory (and trusty_share_memory_compat) will fail instead if the trusty api is too old.",
      "parentUuid": "f0729703_74dd9ae6",
      "revId": "d4f919f386d0d049c2d34f057d0d4db4e1f887f7",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "dcb785c2_ec7d765e",
        "filename": "drivers/trusty/trusty-log.c",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 649,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000205
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-01-26T01:49:59Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Do we need a max? If so, how does this limit compare to other user configurable kernel buffers (e.g. trace buffer, kernel log)",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 649,
        "startChar": 28,
        "endLine": 649,
        "endChar": 48
      },
      "revId": "d4f919f386d0d049c2d34f057d0d4db4e1f887f7",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "81c928b2_a6ac32e1",
        "filename": "drivers/trusty/trusty-log.c",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 649,
      "author": {
        "id": 1001525
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-01-26T03:37:50Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "We don\u0027t *need* a max, other than to avoid overflows when we multiply the parameter value with PAGE_SIZE below. That\u0027s the main reason I put a max at all, and I picked 1MB because that seemed plenty, with 1MB being 64 times larger than the currently used buffer.\nOn the two devices I checked we set the kernel log size to 1 MB using a kernel parameter (up from the compiled-in default of 128 KB).",
      "parentUuid": "dcb785c2_ec7d765e",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 649,
        "startChar": 28,
        "endLine": 649,
        "endChar": 48
      },
      "revId": "d4f919f386d0d049c2d34f057d0d4db4e1f887f7",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "949e635f_82356d6b",
        "filename": "drivers/trusty/trusty-log.c",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 649,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000205
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-01-26T04:00:22Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "OK, but a developer could want a larger size so 1 MB seems like a low limit.",
      "parentUuid": "81c928b2_a6ac32e1",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 649,
        "startChar": 28,
        "endLine": 649,
        "endChar": 48
      },
      "revId": "d4f919f386d0d049c2d34f057d0d4db4e1f887f7",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "99c30160_c67f0a0c",
        "filename": "drivers/trusty/trusty-log.c",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 655,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000205
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-01-26T01:49:59Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Why not round down instead? Also it is possible to set a handler for the param itself",
      "revId": "d4f919f386d0d049c2d34f057d0d4db4e1f887f7",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "c8a3ac67_1ea42a40",
        "filename": "drivers/trusty/trusty-log.c",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 655,
      "author": {
        "id": 1001525
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-01-26T03:37:50Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I wanted to keep it simple. You specify it wrong, you get the default.\nDo you mean a handler to allow setting the parameter at any time? That goes back to \"keep it simple\". Setting the size at run time would require re-allocating the buffer, reclaiming the old buffer from Trusty, setting a new one, and preferably without losing any logs that haven\u0027t been read yet. It just adds a lot of complexity that I don\u0027t think is worth the effort.",
      "parentUuid": "99c30160_c67f0a0c",
      "revId": "d4f919f386d0d049c2d34f057d0d4db4e1f887f7",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "554e2571_608d1289",
        "filename": "drivers/trusty/trusty-log.c",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 655,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000205
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-01-26T04:00:22Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The parameter can already be set at any time, but the way you use it only affects future allocations. Re-allocating a buffer for an existing device would be possible with a handler, but that is not what I was suggesting here. The handler can just validate the value, and the rest of the code stays the same. I don\u0027t like that the caller have to know that the number has to be a power of 2 + 1 page. Rounding down, or up, seems like a friendlier interface. The handler is not strictly needed for that, but it makes the real value you get more visible. Although on a related note, a buffer size with memparse would also be nicer as the kernel then support unit suffixes.",
      "parentUuid": "c8a3ac67_1ea42a40",
      "revId": "d4f919f386d0d049c2d34f057d0d4db4e1f887f7",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "f0caa2ee_7fefbc9d",
        "filename": "drivers/trusty/trusty-log.c",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 655,
      "author": {
        "id": 1001525
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-01-26T05:00:27Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e The parameter can already be set at any time,\n\nHow can it currently be set at any time? The /sys entry is read-only.",
      "parentUuid": "554e2571_608d1289",
      "revId": "d4f919f386d0d049c2d34f057d0d4db4e1f887f7",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "0401b03a_15f90656",
        "filename": "drivers/trusty/trusty-log.c",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 655,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000205
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-01-26T05:16:24Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "OK. In that case it can\u0027t be set at anytime, but the handler could still handle any value passed in to the kernel or module. You don\u0027t need to make this read-only though even if it has no effect until the next time you bind the device?",
      "parentUuid": "f0caa2ee_7fefbc9d",
      "revId": "d4f919f386d0d049c2d34f057d0d4db4e1f887f7",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
